# Queue jobs

One `email_jobs` row and one queued job per recipient. `QUEUE_CONNECTION=database`. Dispatch only after the campaign transaction commits. [ADR-0012](../../docs/adr/0012-smtp-delivery-via-laravel-mailer.md) sends through the Laravel mailer and supersedes the simulated send in ADR-0002.

## Do

- Process pending jobs FIFO.
- Send `CampaignMail` once per recipient through the configured mailer. Do not queue the mailable again.
- Leave the row `pending` when a transport error is retried (3 attempts, 10 s then 30 s). Mark it `failed` only from `failed()`.
- Move the campaign from `queued` to `processing` to `done`.
- Skip a job that is no longer `pending`.
- Pause after a successful send when `MAIL_SEND_INTERVAL_MS` is set.

## Do not

- Add a vendor mail SDK or a second provider strategy.
- Let one recipient failure stop the worker.
- Treat `done` as "every email succeeded". `done` means every job is `sent` or `failed`.

```php
// ✅ GOOD
if ($emailJob->status !== EmailJobStatus::Pending) {
    return;
}

Mail::to($emailJob->recipient_email)->send(new CampaignMail($campaign));
```
